# Authority follows interaction, two guests at one heap: both throw into it at once. Each owns
# what it set going first (the earliest confirmed toucher); a take of a body the other owns is
# refused and the loser's copy is pulled to the winner's.
scenario authority_two_guests
scene load300
seed 63
guests 2
settle 12s
light_mass 20kg
authority interaction

net g1 rtt 100ms jitter 20ms loss 2%
net g2 rtt 250ms jitter 30ms loss 2%

p1 walk load290
p1 grab load290 as a1
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw 0 0.5 0 speed 9 as t1
p2 walk load209
p2 grab load209 as a2
p2 wait 300ms
p2 throw 0 0.5 0 speed 9 as t2

expect result a1 granted
expect result a2 granted
# Derived: at rest each copy lies within the second layer's dead zone of its owner (1 cm, 2 degrees,
# README "The second layer"), as in every layer scene.
expect agree_at_rest 1cm 2deg
expect no_stuck
# Derived: as in authority_host_push, a take keeps the pose: 1 cm.
expect local_correction.max <= 1cm
# Derived: the same correction of its turn. The stand reads an angle through acosf of a float
# dot product, 2 sqrt(2 n 2^-24) rad for a dot n ulps off 1: 0.04 deg a ulp, 0.16 deg at 16,
# which three float products of unit turns stay within; the least turn a placement shows is a
# hundredth of a radian, 0.57 deg: 0.25 deg.
expect local_turn.max <= 0.25deg
# Measured 41 and 56 takes, 6 and 33 refused (seed 63): each guest takes, and a take of what
# the other set going first is refused.
expect takes.count >= 10
expect take_refusals.count >= 1
# Derived: between two take-backs a prediction's pull is paused at most (120 + 60) / 2 of any
# 120 ticks (sync_soft.h: the chain cap 60, drained a tick per tick without a touch): 90.
expect pause_window.max <= 90t
